{
 "id": "T10",
 "title": "Patient lookup: string and identifier search semantics",
 "scenario": "A registration desk integration and a duplicate-patient checker search Patient by name and MRN. Names include accents, a two-part Spanish family name, a hyphenated family name, an old (maiden) name, an honorific prefix and all-caps legacy data. All patients are fictional. You are checking which resources each query returns.",
 "server_timezone": "America/New_York",
 "why_hard": "Default FHIR string search is case- AND accent-insensitive 'starts with' (not contains, not exact) and applies to every HumanName on the resource, including old names; name also covers prefix/suffix/text; family-name parts are searched independently; :contains matches anywhere (still case/accent-insensitive); :exact is case- and accent-sensitive whole-value. Identifier token search compares system and value exactly (no zero-stripping); a bare value matches any system and any identifier type; :of-type needs type system, type code AND value.",
